[[File:Sasamuta jinja Shaden.JPG|thumb|right|Shaden at Sasamuta-jinja]] [[File:Sasamuta mannenbashi.jpg|thumb|right|Man'nenbashi Bridge at Sasamuta Shrine]] {{nihongo|'''Sasamuta-jinja'''|西寒多神社||}} is a [[Japan]]ese [[Shinto shrine]] in [[Oita, Oita]] on the island of [[Kyushu]].<ref name="kotodamayama">Kotodamaya.com, [http://www.kotodamaya.com/sasamuta-jinja/ "Sasamuta Jinja"]; retrieved 2012-10-25.</ref>
Sasamuta was the chief Shinto shrine (''[[ichinomiya]]'') of the old [[Bungo Province]]. It serves today as one of the ''ichinomiya'' of [[Niigata Prefecture]]. <ref>[http://eos.kokugakuin.ac.jp/modules/xwords/images/uploads/EOS070712Ab.pdf "Nationwide List of ''Ichinomiya''," p. 3]; retrieved 2012-10-25.</ref> The enshrined ''[[kami]]'' is: * {{nihongo|Amaterasu oomikami|天照皇大御神||}}<ref name="kotodamayama"/>
==Related pages== * [[List of Shinto shrines in Japan]] * [[Modern system of ranked Shinto Shrines]]
==References== {{reflist}}
==External links == {{Commons category-inline|Sasamuta-jinja}}
